Don't try to unlink an older existing directory when extracting cpio.
For a member whose name exists and is older, data_extract_all() calls
unlink() and accepts EISDIR for a directory, which is what Linux
returns. Windows returns EACCES instead, so a directory entry over an
older existing directory, including "." from find ., ended cpio -i with
"can't remove old file". Don't unlink an existing directory.

---
 archival/libarchive/data_extract_all.c |    6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/archival/libarchive/data_extract_all.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/data_extract_all.c
@@ -130,7 +130,11 @@
 			data_skip(archive_handle);
 			goto ret;
 		}
-		else if ((unlink(dst_name) == -1) && (errno != EISDIR)) {
+		/* Don't try to unlink a directory: that fails with EISDIR
+		 * on Linux, but with other errors elsewhere, e.g. Windows */
+		else if (!S_ISDIR(existing_sb.st_mode)
+		 && unlink(dst_name) == -1
+		) {
 			bb_perror_msg_and_die("can't remove old file %s",
 					dst_name);
 		}
